Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790063999999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": false, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790035199999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The strongest counterargument: the largest single directional move in the window is the opening 12-bar, ~36% bear leg to 1368.42, so the bull-trend label rests only on the last ~34 bars, and the 73 bars before that are balance, not trend.", "The 27 bars ahead of the final push are a two-sided range (2357.18-2680) with heavy overlap and mid-range closes; 2850 is a first-bar probe only 79.00 above 2771, and single-bar breakouts of multi-week range tops often fail and re-enter the range.", "Bar 1787270400000 (445.69 range, close 2515.30, ~255.70 upper tail) followed by a 27-bar stall is spike-high behavior consistent with a temporary exhaustion and a market capped by a range boundary rather than a functioning bull channel.", "The 208.30-point final bar after an extended advance could be a buy climax; a large bull bar that is immediately retraced would mark exhaustion rather than breakout acceptance."], "evidence_for": ["A 388.17-point bull trend bar (1787097600000) closed at 2252.16, 89% of its range and above the 73-bar range top 1974.46, with immediate follow-through to 2771 two bars later.", "Successive higher swing highs across the window (1974.46, 2293.80, 2771, 2850) and higher swing lows (1368.42, 1512.91, 2357.18/2358.62).", "The 27-bar pause held entirely above the breakout bar's open 1916.51 and the old range top 1974.46; no close returned inside the 73-bar range.", "The final bar closes 2775.61 above the prior spike high 2771 and in the upper 64% of its range, with four consecutive rising closes."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["The window opens at 2109.85 (close of 1779667200000) after a 2139.34 high, then declines 13 bars to 1368.42 (low of 1780704000000), about 36% below 2139.34.", "Bar 1780704000000 has a 230.85 range with a 200.13 lower tail and closes at 1568.55 (top ~13% of its range); bar 1780790400000 (open 1568.55, high 1690.78, low 1563.52, close 1687.83) is a bull reversal bar closing at its high.", "From 1780790400000 to 1787011200000 (73 bars) price overlaps repeatedly between 1512.91 (low of 1782432000000) and 1974.46 (high of 1785110400000); closes cluster 1550-1950 with many overlapping bodies and mixed closes (two-sided range).", "Bar 1787097600000 breaks out: open 1916.51, high 2293.80, low 1905.63, close 2252.16, a 388.17-point bull trend bar closing in the top ~11% of its range and above the 1974.46 range top.", "Bar 1787270400000 spikes to 2771 with a 445.69 range, closing 2515.30 and leaving a ~255.70 upper tail.", "Bars 1787184000000 through 1789603200000 (27 bars) stay between 2357.18 (low of 1788307200000) and 2680 (high of 1789084800000); bodies overlap and closes sit mostly 2380-2530.", "The last four closes are 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90, 2775.61; the final bar (open 2642.90, high 2850, low 2641.70, close 2775.61) closes above the prior spike high 2771 in the upper 64% of its 208.30-point range."], "phase": "breakout-spike", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Bear leg of 13 bars from the window high 2139.34 into the 1368.42 low of 1780704000000; bar ranges expand into the low and that bar closes 1568.55 with a 200.13 lower tail, followed by a bull reversal bar at 1687.83.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1779667200000, "upper_boundary": "2139.34"}, {"description": "73-bar two-sided range from 1780790400000 to 1787011200000; repeated overlap between 1512.91 and 1974.46 with a slight upward tilt after the 1512.91 low, many inside bars and closes in the middle of the range.", "end_time_ms": 1787183999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Bull spike escaping the 73-bar range: bar 1787097600000 opens 1916.51 and closes 2252.16 above the 1974.46 range top, with follow-through to the 2771 spike high of 1787270400000.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Post-spike pause of 27 bars between the 2357.18 low of 1788307200000 and the 2680 high of 1789084800000; most highs sit 2520-2560 with probes to 2680 and most lows 2357-2440, heavy body overlap and mid-range closes.", "end_time_ms": 1789689599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787184000000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Final bull leg from the 2358.62 low of bar 1789430400000: 1789689600000 and 1789776000000 close 2612.02 and 2632.98, and 1789948800000 closes 2775.61 above the 2771 spike high. The breakout proper is bars 1789689600000-1789948800000.", "end_time_ms": 1790035199999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Bull continuation: several consecutive closes holding above 2700 (high of 1789776000000) and above 2771, with higher lows above 2641.70, would confirm acceptance above the spike high and strengthen the bull-trend/breakout-spike read.", "Failed breakout: a close back below 2641.70 (low of the final bar), followed by a close below 2568.16 (low of 1789862400000), would signal the breakout failed and shift the read back toward the 2357.18-2680 range.", "Range reassertion: a close back below 2357.18 with follow-through would turn the post-spike structure into a top and recast the 1787097600000 advance as a bull trap.", "Trend weakening: deeper pullbacks that overlap prior swing lows together with more bear bars closing near their lows would move the phase from breakout-spike toward channel or range.", "Climax risk: a further outsized bull bar immediately followed by a bear bar closing near its low would argue for a buy climax rather than a sustained second leg."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790049599999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Roughly the first 78 of 120 bars (bars 0-77) were two-sided inside 2357.18-2700.00 with heavy overlap, so the trend evidence rests on the last ~38 bars of a window that was mostly a trading range.", "Bar 115 closed at only about 34% of its own 191.94 range with a 126.85 upper tail, so it was not a strong close-at-high breakout bar.", "Two earlier spikes failed in the same location: bar 56 reached 2680.00 and closed 2555.52, and bar 103 reached 2700 and closed 2638.49, each followed by a slide toward 2500-2570.", "Bar 119 (open 2775.60, close 2738.87, low 2727.22) is a bear bar closing near its low and erasing the closes of bars 116-118, leaving the last four bars overlapping in the 2718.09-2804.59 band.", "No bar has closed above 2804.59 and the breakout is only about five bars old, so acceptance above the old range top is unproven; volume on bar 115 (8.43M) is below the window's heaviest prints.", "An equally plausible reading is that bars 115-119 are a final flag / exhaustion pause at the top of a 20-day range rather than the start of a sustained bull trend; nothing has yet broken down to confirm that alternative."], "evidence_for": ["Bar 115 broke above the 2700 top that had capped bars 0-113 and exceeded both earlier failed spike highs (2680.00 on bar 56, 2700 on bars 103 and 113), making a new window high at 2850.00.", "Follow-through differs from the earlier failures: bars 116-118 all closed above bar 115's 2723.15 close, whereas bar 56 was followed immediately by bar 57 (open 2557.34, close 2538.73) giving back the spike.", "Multi-leg advance since bar 81 shows higher lows (2435.71 bar 92, 2568.16 bar 109, 2718.09 bar 116) and higher highs (2643.52 bar 99, 2700 bar 103, 2850.00 bar 115), i.e., more than a single leg.", "The bars 107-109 pullback ended with a doji at 2568.16 (bar 109) and bar 110 closed on its high 2611.00, a bull reversal bar that began the final advance.", "At the decision time no bar has closed back inside the pre-breakout range; price remains above the 2700 breakout level."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window is 120 closed H4 bars (about 20 days), open_time 1788321600000 to close_time 1790049599999; window low is 2357.18 (bar 1 low) and window high is 2850.00 (bar 115 high).", "Bars 0-112 mostly traded inside 2357.18-2700.00: bar 8 (open 2407.48, close 2506.79) spiked up but bar 14 (open 2523.22, low 2436.73, close 2450.96) reversed it; bar 56 (open 2457.12, high 2680, low 2444.19, close 2555.52) had a 235.81 range and gave back 124.48 from its high.", "The 2700 level was tested exactly on bar 103 (high 2700, close 2638.49) and bar 113 (high 2700, close 2664.73) and was rejected both times.", "Bar 81 (low 2358.62) retested bar 1's 2357.18 low; afterwards lows rose (2384.29 bar 86, 2435.71 bar 92, 2568.16 bar 109, 2718.09 bar 116) and highs rose (2481.66 bar 92, 2643.52 bar 99, 2700 bar 103, 2850.00 bar 115).", "Bars 107-109 pulled back to 2568.16; bar 109 (open 2576.97, low 2568.16, close 2577.88) is a small doji and bar 110 closed exactly on its high 2611.00, starting the final leg.", "Bar 115 (open 2658.81, low 2658.06, high 2850.00, close 2723.15) is the tallest bar near the end of the window; its close sits at about 34% of its 191.94 range, leaving a 126.85 upper tail.", "Bars 116-118 closed higher (2754.31, 2760.51, 2775.61) and stayed above bar 115's close; bar 119 (open 2775.60, high 2776.18, low 2727.22, close 2738.87) is a bear bar closing near its low.", "Bars 116-119 overlap in a tight 2718.09-2804.59 band; the window closes at 2738.87, which is 111.13 below the 2850.00 high and 38.87 above the 2700 level.", "Volume on breakout bar 115 (8,427,249.993) is below the window's largest prints (10,757,237.648 on bar 56, 10,207,100.424 on bar 81); volume is optional here and is not treated as required confirmation."], "phase": "breakout-spike", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Broad two-sided range covering most of the window: repeated overlapping swings between the 2357.18 window low (bar 1) and the 2700 top tested on bars 103 and 113, including the failed spike to 2680.00 on bar 56 and the return to the 2500 area on bar 57.", "end_time_ms": 1789991999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1788321600000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "Rising leg off the 2358.62 low (bar 81) with overlapping pullbacks rather than a clean spike: higher lows 2435.71 (bar 92) and 2568.16 (bar 109), higher highs 2643.52 (bar 99) and 2804.59 (bar 118). It stayed inside the 2357.18-2700 range until bars 115-118.", "end_time_ms": 1790049599999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2804.59"}, {"description": "Bull breakout above the 2700 range top on bar 115 (open 2658.81, high 2850.00, close 2723.15), with bars 116-118 closing above the breakout bar's close and holding above 2700. Breakout is about five bars old at the decision time.", "end_time_ms": 1790049599999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2700", "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Tight four-bar overlap (bars 116-119) between 2718.09 and 2804.59 just below the 2850.00 spike high; a pause at the breakout level that is either an early bull flag or the start of a failed breakout back into the old range.", "end_time_ms": 1790049599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2718.09", "start_time_ms": 1789992000000, "upper_boundary": "2804.59"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["Bull confirmation: a close above 2804.59 (bar 118 high) and then above 2850.00 (bar 115 high) would show acceptance of the range breakout and support continuation of the bull trend in spike phase.", "Failed breakout: a close back below 2700 would signal rejection of the breakout level, and a close below bar 115's low 2658.06 would confirm a failed range breakout and shift the read toward trading-range/two-sided.", "Trend damage: a close below 2568.16 (bar 109 low) would end the higher-low sequence running from bar 92 and move the read toward transition-unclear.", "Pause resolution: continued overlapping bars inside 2718.09-2804.59 with no new high would reclassify the current phase as a channel/pause and reduce always-in relevance, while a close above 2804.59 would extend the spike.", "A pullback that holds above 2804.59 after a new high above 2850.00 would mark the first higher low of a confirmed bull channel."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "stale"}}, "raw": {"H1": [{"close": "2444.93", "close_time_ms": 1789635599999, "high": "2445.38", "low": "2436.78", "open": "2442.18", "open_time_ms": 1789632000000, "volume": "1895565.318"}, {"close": "2438.54", "close_time_ms": 1789639199999, "high": "2447.67", "low": "2437.42", "open": "2444.93", "open_time_ms": 1789635600000, "volume": "1437852.631"}, {"close": "2434.35", "close_time_ms": 1789642799999, "high": "2438.6", "low": "2430.62", "open": "2438.54", "open_time_ms": 1789639200000, "volume": "1608938.654"}, {"close": "2438.84", "close_time_ms": 1789646399999, "high": "2438.84", "low": "2427.28", "open": "2434.35", "open_time_ms": 1789642800000, "volume": "2000682.265"}, {"close": "2459.02", "close_time_ms": 1789649999999, "high": "2473.3", "low": "2438.5", "open": "2438.59", "open_time_ms": 1789646400000, "volume": "2142684.217"}, {"close": "2460", "close_time_ms": 1789653599999, "high": "2463.35", "low": "2435.71", "open": "2459